====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable|hyperbole|figuratively}} A place or situation of great suffering in life.
#: {{ux|en|My new boss is making my job a '''hell'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|I went through '''hell''' to get home today.}}
#: {{ux|en|[[callback]] '''hell'''; <code><<nowiki/>[[w:HTML table|table]]></code> '''hell'''; <code><<nowiki/>[[w:span and div|div]]></code> '''hell'''|q=computer programming}}
#* '''1879''', General William T. Sherman, commencement address at the Michigan Military Academy
#*: {{quote|en|There is many a boy here today who looks on war as all glory, but, boys, it is all '''hell'''.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1986|composer=Metallica|title=Disposable Heroes|album=Master of Puppets|passage=Why, am I dying? / Kill, have no fear / Lie, live off lying / '''Hell''', '''hell''' is here}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[place#Noun|place]] for [[gambling#Noun|gambling]].
#* {{RQ:Thackeray Pendennis||passage=Here’s five-and-twenty for you. Don’t be losing it at the '''hells''' now.|61}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1877|author={{w|William Black (novelist)|William Black}}|title=Green Pastures and Piccadilly
|passage=a convenient little gambling '''hell''' for those who had grown reckless}}
#* {{RQ:Conrad Secret Agent|chapter=II|page=15|passage=But there was also about him an indescribable air which no mechanic could have acquired in the practice of his handicraft however dishonestly exercised: [...] the air of moral nihilism common to keepers of gambling '''hells''' and disorderly houses; [...]}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} An [[extremely]] [[hot]] place.
#: {{ux|en|You don’t have a [[snowball's chance in hell|snowball's chance in '''hell''']].}}
# {{lb|en|sometimes considered|_|vulgar}} {{non-gloss definition|Used as an {{glossary|intensifier}} in phrases grammatically requiring a noun.}}
#: {{ux|en|I’m as mad as '''hell''' and I’m not going to take it any more.}}
#: {{ux|en|[[what the hell|What the '''hell''']] is wrong with you?!}}
#: {{ux|en|He says he’s going home early? [[like hell|Like '''hell''']] he is.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A place into which a [[tailor]] [[throw#Verb|throws]] [[shred#Noun|shreds]], or a [[printer]] [[discard#Verb|discards]] [[broken]] [[type#Noun|type]].
#* {{RQ:Butler Hudibras|passage=This sturdy Squire, he had, as well <br>As the bold Trojan Knight, seen '''Hell'''.}}
# In certain [[game]]s of [[chase]], a place to which those who are caught are carried for [[detention]]. <!--Webster 1913-->
# {{lb|en|colloquial|with ''[[on]]''}} Something extremely painful or harmful (to)
#: {{ux|en|That steep staircase is '''hell''' on my knees.}}

